## Summary

This PR extends the modelwise reload prototype into a manifest-driven streaming reload path for dense, quantized, and MoE checkpoints.

The implementation:

- lazily materializes only checkpoint bindings needed by received sources;
- supports arbitrary checkpoint chunks and rank-sharding manifests;
- tracks complete/incomplete module coverage and allows partial-layer updates;
- supports repeated updates for the same MoE expert and generic dense/linear parameters;
- defers model-wide PWAL until `finish_weight_update` and validates that all dependencies of every complete module are materialized;
- restores untouched/skipped runtime bindings, including deferred attention/HPC state;
- validates residual meta bindings with module ownership/state auditing and fails closed for active PWAL dependencies;
- preserves runtime storage identity and supports FP8, compressed-tensors, and packed NCCL checkpoint transfer.

## Validation

Local focused tests:

```text
26 passed
```

Additional reload/weight-transfer tests, Ruff, format checks, and `git diff --check` passed.

H200 end-to-end validation with `vllm-rl-day0-kit` and packed NCCL checkpoint transfer, TP=2:

- Qwen3 dense FP8: output/tokens/logprobs identical before and after reload;
- Qwen3 MoE FP8: output/tokens/logprobs identical before and after reload;
- cut-layer Qwen3.8-27B-FP8: output/tokens/logprobs identical before and after reload;
- cut-layer Kimi K3 dense: output/tokens/logprobs identical before and after reload;
- cut-layer Kimi K3 8-expert MXFP4 MoE: output/tokens/logprobs identical before and after reload;
- all tested `finish_weight_update` calls returned HTTP 200;
- complete-module audits reported `noncomplete=[]` and no active-PWAL residual meta dependencies.

## Relationship to existing reload work

Open PR #51378 covers the earlier modelwise transaction prototype. This branch is intentionally a follow-up with a materially different implementation scope: it adds manifest-driven lazy/streaming
